Of course, they do.  But giving that potion in the hands of monsters 
would be horrible :-).  Wielding it in attack would be impossible unless 
you create a countering ring (such as free action for paralysis) and 
throwing it would be too dangerous, in case you miss and it is thrown 
back at you.

You see, I was discussing a suggestion concerning a potion possibly 
*useful* for a player.  When your suggestion came up, I did not realize 
that it was meant only to work *against* the player.  I am not masochist 
enough to suggest things the only effect of which would be making the 
game harder at all stages.  Since it is pretty well-balanced already, I 
think new suggestions should make life easier at a cost or life more 
difficult at a benefit.  Or remedy an awkward or improvable general 
situation.

Of course, your potion would provide the benefit of being eligible to be 
turned into water.  But that seems too small a benefit to justify its 
introduction.  Also, if the frequencies of other potions are adjusted 
accordingly, one might end up with no benefit at all.
